          "fields": {
            "display_title": "A deep learning model is proposed for dialogue systems that takes advantage of visual information. The proposed method is the straightforward implementation of known models, and the evaluation is purely qualitative in a non standard scenario. ",
            "replying_to": "Replying to Associative Conversation Model: Generating Visual Information from Textual Information"
          }
        },
        {
          "note_id": "SJ4THI9gG",
          "fields": {
            "display_title": "The paper proposes a novel dataset for grounded dialog and suggests that one should reason about vision even when performing text-based dialog. While the idea is intuitive the execution is currently lacking in multiple respects and would benefit from a major revision.",
            "replying_to": "Replying to Associative Conversation Model: Generating Visual Information from Textual Information"
          }
        },
        {
          "note_id": "BkC87_Cgz",
          "fields": {
            "display_title": "The paper's main idea is interesting, and fairly well-explained.  However, outside of a couple of simple, interesting examples, no real validation of the technique is done, and therefore its value is not clear.",
